kanon lean DIR writes the Lean files that it generates for the root R of a
module under DIR/Generated/R/, and the hand-written files of R go in DIR/R
(DIR/R/Sem.lean, DIR/R/Proofs.lean, ...). Everything under DIR/Generated/R is
generated, and nothing outside is written by kanon.

  $ kanon lean out lang.knl
  $ ls out out/Generated out/Generated/Ex
  out:
  Generated
  
  out/Generated:
  Ex
  
  out/Generated/Ex:
  Int
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean
  $ find out/Generated/Ex/Int -type f | sort
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Lang.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Lift.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Model.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Node.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Soundness.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Soundness/Comm.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Soundness/Int/neg.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Soundness/Int/plus.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Statements/Comm.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Statements/Int/neg.lean
  out/Generated/Ex/Int/Statements/Int/plus.lean
  $ head -n 3 out/Generated/Ex/Rules.lean
  -- Generated by kanon from lang.knl, int.knl. Do not edit.
  import Generated.Ex.Semantics
  import Generated.Ex.Int.Soundness

A hand-written file in the directory of its root is imported by the generated
ones, and is never touched.

  $ mkdir -p out/Ex/Int
  $ echo 'import Generated.Ex.Int.Node' > out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean
  $ echo '-- A file of mine.' > out/Ex/Mine.lean
  $ kanon lean out lang.knl
  $ grep '^import Ex.Int.Sem' out/Generated/Ex/Int/Lang.lean
  import Ex.Int.Sem
  $ cat out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean out/Ex/Mine.lean
  import Generated.Ex.Int.Node
  -- A file of mine.

With --check, kanon lean checks that Generated/R has exactly the files that
it would write, for each root R, and nothing else.

  $ kanon lean --check out lang.knl

A file that is missing, one that was edited, and any other file, of any name,
whatever its first line, are reported.

  $ rm out/Generated/Ex/Rules.lean
  $ echo '-- edited' >> out/Generated/Ex/Syntax.lean
  $ mkdir -p out/Generated/Ex/Old
  $ echo '-- Generated by kanon from int.kn. Do not edit.' > out/Generated/Ex/Old/Gone.lean
  $ echo 'mine' > out/Generated/Ex/notes.txt
  $ kanon lean --check out lang.knl
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Syntax.lean is not up to date (run kanon lean)
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Rules.lean is missing (run kanon lean)
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Old/Gone.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean)
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/notes.txt is no longer generated (run kanon lean)
  [1]

kanon lean removes the whole Generated/R directory of each root R before it
writes it again, but nothing else.

  $ kanon lean out lang.knl
  $ kanon lean --check out lang.knl
  $ ls out/Ex out/Generated/Ex
  out/Ex:
  Int
  Mine.lean
  
  out/Generated/Ex:
  Int
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean
  $ cat out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean out/Ex/Mine.lean
  import Generated.Ex.Int.Node
  -- A file of mine.

The files are the same, byte for byte, when Generated is deleted and written
again.

  $ cp -r out out.bak
  $ rm -r out/Generated
  $ kanon lean --check out lang.knl 2>&1 | head -n 2
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Node.lean is missing (run kanon lean)
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Lang.lean is missing (run kanon lean)
  $ kanon lean out lang.knl
  $ diff -r out out.bak

A function or a rule that is removed leaves no stale file.

  $ mkdir fewer && cp lang.knl int.knl fewer && sed '/^rule neg/,$d' int.kn > fewer/int.kn
  $ kanon lean --check out fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | grep neg
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Int/Soundness/Int/neg.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean)
  kanon: out/Generated/Ex/Int/Statements/Int/neg.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean)
  $ kanon lean out fewer/lang.knl
  $ find out -name 'neg.lean' -o -name 'Sem.lean' -o -name 'Mine.lean' | sort
  out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean
  out/Ex/Mine.lean
  $ kanon lean --check out fewer/lang.knl
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ echo '-- Generated by kanon from int.kn. Do not edit.' > out2/Generated/Ex/Removed.lean
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ ls out2/Generated/Ex
  Int
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean

The roots that are not generated are not touched, even if they are in
Generated.

  $ mkdir -p out2/Generated/Other && echo x > out2/Generated/Other/x.lean
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ cat out2/Generated/Other/x.lean
  x

kanon lean does not delete through a symbolic link, nor a file: it fails
before it writes or deletes anything.

  $ mkdir elsewhere && echo precious > elsewhere/file
  $ rm -r out2/Generated/Ex && ln -s ../../elsewhere out2/Generated/Ex
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Generated/Ex is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ kanon lean --check out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Generated/Ex is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ cat elsewhere/file
  precious
  $ ls elsewhere
  file
  $ rm out2/Generated/Ex && echo x > out2/Generated/Ex
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Generated/Ex is not a directory
  [1]
  $ cat out2/Generated/Ex
  x
  $ rm out2/Generated/Ex && mkdir out2/Generated/Ex
  $ mv out2/Generated out2/Generated.real && ln -s Generated.real out2/Generated
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Generated is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ rm out2/Generated && mv out2/Generated.real out2/Generated

A symbolic link inside Generated/R is removed, not followed.

  $ ln -s ../../../elsewhere out2/Generated/Ex/link
  $ kanon lean --check out2 fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | grep link
  kanon: out2/Generated/Ex/link is no longer generated (run kanon lean)
  $ kanon lean out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ ls elsewhere out2/Generated/Ex
  elsewhere:
  file
  
  out2/Generated/Ex:
  Int
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean

DIR is a directory, and is created if it does not exist, as there is nothing to
delete then. A root does not start with Generated, which is the directory of the
generated files.

  $ echo x > afile
  $ kanon lean afile fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: afile is not a directory
  [1]
  $ kanon lean --check newdir fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | head -n 1
  kanon: newdir/Generated/Ex/Node.lean is missing (run kanon lean)
  $ test -e newdir || echo not created
  not created
  $ printf '[@@@lean_root "Generated.Ex"]\nsort TA\nnode A of int : TA\n' > gen.knl
  $ kanon lean out3 gen.knl
  kanon: the root "Generated.Ex" of the module Gen starts with Generated, the directory of the generated files
  [1]
  $ test -e out3 || echo nothing written
  nothing written
